  * Reject ignored client options and write CSV for --csv -o.
  * Resolve hostnames asynchronously inside the connect deadline.
  * Check destination write access before replacing saved files.
  * Preserve errors and final averages in compact client views.
  * Apply destination permissions when creating temporary saves.
  * Bound metrics headers and connection lifetimes.
  * Keep throughput and help accessible in small terminals.
  * Lock update-check settings controlled by higher-priority
