Tue Jul  7 07:42:24 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 0.9.21:
  Security
  * Preset allowlists are now enforced by xfr serve --preset.
  * PSK handling is stricter and safer by default.
  * PSK sessions now require AEAD-protected control channels.
  Fixed
  * Dual-stack sockets now apply address-family policy consistently
  * Cancel, MPTCP validation, and the QUIC UDP tee no longer spin
    on closed or diverted channels.
  * Client control reads no longer desynchronize on cancel or pause
  * Pause time is excluded from test clocks.
  * Cancel and pause take effect immediately on the server.
  * UDP paced sender no longer bursts after resume.
  * Pause channel closure and QUIC task teardown.
  * TCP send paths no longer replay bytes after short writes.
  * Server active-test state is cleaned up on abort, cancel, and
    early error.
  * Server final TCP_INFO now aggregates all TCP streams.
  * TCP RTT averages no longer truncate fractional microseconds.
  * Diff zero baselines now register as regressions.
  * Push Gateway timeout no longer silently dropped.
  * JSON output now propagates serialization errors.
  * Push Gateway metrics emit # HELP/# TYPE once per family.
  * Malformed protocol versions are no longer treated as compatible
  * Receive-side TCP resets at normal teardown are treated as EOF
    without hiding mid-test failures.
  * Socket buffer tuning once again degrades gracefully on OS
    rejection.
  * xfr diff no longer fails default comparisons on tiny TCP metric
    noise.
  * Server bidirectional TCP no longer double-counts send-half
    retransmits.
  * Failed tests are distinct in the server TUI.
  * Bare-major protocol versions are accepted again.
  * TestAck and MTU probe packets reject invalid wire shapes.
  * MTU probing handles echo-only success and IPv6 literals
    correctly.
  * TUI average speed and retransmit fallback are no longer biased.
  * Server preset max duration is applied with CLI precedence.
  * Explicit --probe-mtu -t 10s duration is preserved.
  * IPv6 MTU probe ladder uses IPv6 overhead for both bounds.
  Maintenance
  * Rate-limit integration coverage now asserts rejection.
  * --no-default-features no longer warns on the mDNS fallback stub

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Jun 23 20:37:09 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update version 0.9.20:
  * Updated 'quinn-proto' to 0.11.15 to address [RUSTSEC-2026-0185]
    (https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0185) (High, 7.5),
    a remote memory-exhaustion denial of service in QUIC stream
    reassembly, where unbounded buffering of out-of-order stream
    data could let a peer drive a server's memory usage without
    bound. This affects xfr's QUIC server path (any host running
    'xfr -s' reachable by an untrusted QUIC client). Lockfile-only
    update — no source or API changes, and no configuration change
    is required.

